==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|defendor|defendour||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|xno|defendour}}, from {{der|en|fro|defendeor}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/dɪˈfɛndə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-defender.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛndə(ɹ)}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|defender (football)}}
{{en-noun}}

# someone who [[defend]]s [[people]] or [[property]]
# {{lb|en|sports}} one of the [[players]] whose primary task is to [[prevent]] the opposition from [[scoring]]
# a [[fighter]] who seeks to [[repel]] an [[attack]]
# {{lb|en|law|rare}} a [[lawyer]] who [[represent]]s [[defendant]]s, especially a [[public defender]]; a [[defense attorney]] (US) or [[defence counsel]] (UK)
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1822|title=A Complete Collection of State Trials and Proceedings for High Treason and Other Crimes and Misdemeanors from the Earliest Period to the Year 1783 |author=Thomas Bayly Howell   |page=729 |ISBN= |passage=There was another protection to which she was intitled by that law, namely, a '''defender'''; but she had none. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|title=Continuing the Struggle for Justice |author=Barry Krisberg, ‎Susan Marchionna, ‎& Christopher Baird  |page=248 |ISBN=1452278954 |passage=So, what is contemplated under this model is that the '''defender''' would work with civil legal services lawyers to address the clients'  needs. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|title=Effective Depositions  |author=Henry L. Hecht  |page=243 |ISBN=1604429062 |passage=It puts you at the head of the table, at a right angle to the witness; the court reporter sits to your right, and the '''defender''' sits on the witness's far side. }}
# {{lb|en|Scotland|law}} a [[defendant]] in a civil action

